{"docid": "30112107", "title": "Coburg Peak", "uri": "Q5139027", "text": "Coburg Peak (, ) is the rocky peak rising to 783 m in Erul Heights on Trinity Peninsula in Graham Land, Antarctica. It is surmounting Cugnot Ice Piedmont to the northeast.\n\nThe peak is named after the Bulgarian royal house of Coburg (Saxe-Coburg-Gotha), 1887–1946.", "entities": [{"uri": "Q5395951", "boundaries": [54, 66], "surfaceform": "Erul Heights", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q2038835", "boundaries": [70, 87], "surfaceform": "Trinity Peninsula", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q618370", "boundaries": [91, 102], "surfaceform": "Graham Land", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q51", "boundaries": [104, 114], "surfaceform": "Antarctica", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q5192667", "boundaries": [134, 153], "surfaceform": "Cugnot Ice Piedmont", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q164950", "boundaries": [211, 222], "surfaceform": "royal house", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q4996295", "boundaries": [234, 251], "surfaceform": "Saxe-Coburg-Gotha", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "Q5139027", "boundaries": [0, 11], "surfaceform": "Coburg Peak", "annotator": "Me"}, {"uri": "1887-01-01T00:00:00Z^^http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime", "boundaries": [254, 258], "surfaceform": "1887", "annotator": "Date_Linker"}, {"uri": "+1946^^http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal", "boundaries": [259, 263], "surfaceform": "1946", "annotator": "Value_Linker"}], "triples": [{"subject": {"uri": "Q2038835", "boundaries": [70, 87], "surfaceform": "Trinity Peninsula", "annotator": "Me"}, "predicate": {"uri": "P361", "boundaries": null, "surfaceform": "part of", "annotator": "Simple-Aligner"}, "object": {"uri": "Q618370", "boundaries": [91, 102], "surfaceform": "Graham Land", "annotator": "Me"}, "sentence_id": 0, "dependency_path": null, "confidence": null, "annotator": "Simple-Aligner"}, {"subject": {"uri": "Q2038835", "boundaries": [70, 87], "surfaceform": "Trinity Peninsula", "annotator": "Me"}, "predicate": {"uri": "P30", "boundari